WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
One line of maths on a
whiteboard: eight divided by two,

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.460
then two, bracket, two plus two.

3
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.180
On the left, a student works
through it and circles one.

4
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.990
On the right, another student,
just as confident, circles sixteen.

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.390
Same numbers, same symbols.

6
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.760
So which is right?

7
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.950
Or could both be correct?

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.560
In this mission, you'll learn the
rules for which step comes first,

9
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.320
starting with brackets.

10
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.550
You'll see what a number
written next to a bracket means.

11
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.730
And you'll find out why multiplication
and division share the same rank,

12
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.050
and are worked from left to right.

13
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.610
Your mission: decide whether
eight divided by two,

14
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.280
bracket two plus two,
gives one or sixteen.
